<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pamheiba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1709–1748</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Garib Niwaz, Gharib Nawaz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pamheiba, known as Garib Niwaz, was king of Manipur from 1709 to 1748. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaishnavism">Vaishnavism</a> the court religion, reportedly ordering the burning of older Meitei scriptures, and led repeated campaigns into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, raiding deep into the Irrawaddy valley. His reign marked the height of Manipur's military power.</p></div>
